<article class="env-lemma" id="05T0">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05T0">Lemma <span data-tag="05T0">13.14.13</span>.</a> Assumptions and notation as in Situation <a href="/tag/05S8" data-tag="05S8">13.14.1</a>. Let $X, Y$ be objects of $\mathcal{D}$. If $X \oplus Y$ computes $RF$, then $X$ and $Y$ compute $RF$. Similarly for $LF$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      If $X \oplus Y$ computes $RF$, then $RF(X \oplus Y) = F(X) \oplus F(Y)$. In the proof of Lemma <a href="/tag/05SD" data-tag="05SD">13.14.7</a> we have seen that the functor $X/S \times Y/S \to (X \oplus Y)/S$, $(s, s') \mapsto s \oplus s'$ is cofinal. Thus by Categories, Lemma <a href="/tag/0A1S" data-tag="0A1S">4.22.11</a> and by characterization (4) of Categories, Lemma <a href="/tag/05PY" data-tag="05PY">4.22.9</a> we know that for any object $W$ in $\mathcal{D}'$ the map 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{\mathcal{D}'}(F(X \oplus Y), W) \longrightarrow \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits _{s : X \to X', s' : Y \to Y'} \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{\mathcal{D}'}(F(X' \oplus Y'), W)  \]
</div>
    <p>
       is bijective. Since this arrow is clearly compatible with direct sum decompositions on both sides, we conclude that the map 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{\mathcal{D}'}(F(X), W) \longrightarrow \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits _{s : X \to X'} \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{\mathcal{D}'}(F(X'), W)  \]
</div>
    <p>
       is bijective (minor detail omitted). Thus by Categories, Lemma <a href="/tag/05PY" data-tag="05PY">4.22.9</a> we conclude $RF$ is defined at $X$ with value $F(X)$. Similarly for $Y$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>